hadiths[25]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2069","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed: ""O Allah! Make the sustenance of Muhammad's (peace be upon him) family sufficient for their needs."""
"2070","Sayyidah ‘Urwah narrates from Umm al-Mu’minin ‘A’ishah Siddiqah (may Allah be pleased with her) that she used to say: ""By Allah, O my nephew! We would see one crescent, then another, then a third, thus in two months we would see three crescents, and no fire would be lit in the houses of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) during that time."" I said, ""O aunt! Then what was your sustenance?"" She said, ""Dates and water. However, some neighbors of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) from among the Ansar had milch animals, and they would send milk to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he would give us that milk to drink."""
"2071","Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away, and he never ate his fill of bread and olive oil twice in one day (that is, he never ate his fill in both the morning and evening)."
"2072","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the family of Muhammad (peace be upon him) was never satisfied with wheat bread for two consecutive days; sometimes only dates were available for a day."
"2073","Sayyiduna Abu Hazim says: I saw Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) repeatedly gesturing with his two fingers and saying, ""By Him in Whose hand is the life of Abu Hurairah! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and his family never ate their fill of wheat bread for three consecutive days, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) departed from this world."""
"2074","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away and there were a few handfuls of barley in my container. I used to eat from it. Many days passed like this. (Then) I measured it, and it finished. (It became clear that there is more blessing in an unknown and unspecified thing.)"
"2075","Sayyiduna Simak bin Harb says that I heard Sayyiduna Nu'man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) delivering a sermon, he was saying that Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) mentioned the (wealth and riches) that people were acquiring, and then said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would remain restless from hunger all day, and even inferior dates would not be available to him with which he could fill his stomach."
"2076","Sayyiduna Abu Abdur Rahman Hubli says: I heard from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-As (may Allah be pleased with him), and a person asked him, ""Are we not among the poor emigrants?"" Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Do you have a wife with whom you live?"" He replied, ""Yes, I have."" Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Do you have a house in which you live?"" He replied, ""Yes, I have."" Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Then you are among the rich."" He said, ""I also have a servant."" Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Then you are among the kings."" Abu Abdur Rahman said: Three men came to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) while I was present with him. They said, ""O Muhammad! By Allah, we have nothing available to us—neither expenses, nor ride, nor provisions."" Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Whatever you wish, I will do. If you wish, come to us, and we will give you what Allah has written in your destiny. And if you wish, we will mention your case to the king. And if you wish, be patient, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'The needy emigrants will enter Paradise forty years before the wealthy.'"" They said, ""We will be patient and ask for nothing."""
"2077","Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I stood at the gate of Paradise and saw that most of those who entered it were the poor, while the wealthy were held back for account (whereas the believing poor had already entered Paradise without reckoning), and those destined for Hell had already been ordered to Hell. And I stood at the gate of Hell and saw that most of those entering it were women."
"2078","Narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed through the market and he was coming to Madinah from the direction of ‘Aliyah, and people were on one or both sides of him. He (peace be upon him) saw a dead lamb with small ears or with cut ears. He (peace be upon him) took hold of its ear, then said: “Who among you would take this for one dirham?” The people said: “We would not want it for anything, even for one dirham (i.e., in exchange for anything), and what would we do with it?” He (peace be upon him) said: “Would you like it to be yours?” The people said: “By Allah, even if it were alive, it would have a defect, as its ears are very small; then it is dead, so who would take it?” He (peace be upon him) said: “By Allah, the world is more insignificant to Allah than this is to you.”"
"2079","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The world is a prison for the believer and a paradise for the disbeliever."
"2080","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Amr bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Sayyiduna Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah (may Allah be pleased with him) to Bahrain to collect the jizya from there, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had made peace with the people of Bahrain and had appointed Sayyiduna Alaa bin Hadrami (may Allah be pleased with him) as their governor. Then Sayyiduna Abu Ubaidah (may Allah be pleased with him) brought that wealth from Bahrain. This news reached the Ansar, so they performed the Fajr prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he finished the prayer and turned around, the Ansar came before him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled when he saw them and said, ""I think you have heard that Abu Ubaidah has brought some wealth from Bahrain?"" (And you have gathered today with the thought that you will receive some wealth.) They said, ""Indeed, O Messenger of Allah!"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Rejoice and hope for that which will make you happy. By Allah! I do not fear poverty for you, but I fear that the world will be opened up for you as it was opened up for those before you, and you will compete with one another for it as those before you competed, and it will destroy you as it destroyed them."""
"2081","´Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When Persia and Rome are conquered, what will you say? Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We will say what Allah has commanded us (that is, we will give thanks for it). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: And you will say nothing else? You will envy, then you will be jealous, then you will break ties with your friends, then you will become enemies, or he said something similar. Then you will go to the poor emigrants and appoint one of them as ruler over the others."
"2082","Sayyiduna Mustawraq bin Fihir says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, the world in comparison to the Hereafter is like if one of you were to dip his finger into the river (and Yahya pointed with his index finger), then see how much moisture he brings back from it. (So the amount of water that remains on the finger is like the world, and the river is like the Hereafter. This is the proportion of the world to the Hereafter, and since the world is perishable and the Hereafter is everlasting, therefore it is even less than that.)"
"2083","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who used to say: Among the people of Bani Israel, there were three men—one was a leper, the second was bald, and the third was blind. So Allah Almighty wished to test them, and He sent an angel to them. The angel came to the leper and said, ""Which thing is most beloved to you?"" He replied, ""A good color, good skin, and that this disease be removed from me because of which people dislike me."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angel passed his hand over him, so his ugliness was removed and he was given a good color and good skin. The angel said, ""Which wealth do you like most?"" He said, ""Camels or cows."" (The narrator of the hadith, Ishaq bin Abdullah, is in doubt whether he asked for camels or cows, but either the leper or the bald one said camels and the other said cows.) So he was given a pregnant she-camel of ten months, and it was said, ""May Allah bless this for you."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then the angel came to the bald man and said, ""Which thing is most beloved to you?"" He replied, ""Good hair, and that this disease be removed from me because of which people dislike me."" Then the angel passed his hand over him, so his disease was removed and he was given good hair. The angel said, ""Which wealth do you like most?"" He said, ""Cows."" So he was given a pregnant cow. The angel said, ""May Allah bless your wealth."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then the angel came to the blind man and said, ""Which thing is most beloved to you?"" He replied, ""That Allah restores my eyesight so that I may see people."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then the angel passed his hand over him, so Allah restored his eyesight. The angel said, ""Which wealth do you like most?"" He said, ""Sheep and goats."" So he was given a pregnant goat. Then both (the she-camel and the cow) and this (goat) gave birth. Eventually, the leper had a valley full of camels, the bald man had a valley full of cows and oxen, and the blind man had a valley full of sheep and goats. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: After some time, the same angel came to the leper in his original form and appearance and said, ""I am a poor man; all my means have been exhausted during my journey (that is, I have no resources left, nor wealth or belongings), so today, except for Allah's help and then your help, it is not possible for me to reach my destination. I ask you, by Him who gave you a good color and good skin and wealth—camels—for one camel that may help me in my journey."" He replied, ""I have many obligations to people (that is, I am in debt or do not have more wealth than is needed for my household expenses to give you)."" Then the angel said, ""I recognize you. Were you not a poor leper, whom people disliked? Then Allah, by His grace, gave you this wealth."" He replied, ""I inherited this wealth from my forefathers, passed down through generations."" The angel said, ""If you are lying, may Allah return you to what you were before."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then the angel came to the bald man in his original form and appearance and said to him the same as he had said to the leper, and he also gave the same answer as the leper had given. The angel said, ""If you are lying, may Allah return you to what you were before."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then the angel came to the blind man in his original form and appearance and said, ""I am a poor man and a traveler; all my means and resources have been exhausted during my journey, so today, except for Allah's help and then your help, it is difficult for me to reach my destination. So I ask you, by Allah who gave you eyesight, for one goat so that it may help me in my journey."" He replied, ""Indeed, I was blind, so Allah gave me (eyes with) sight. So take from these goats as many as you wish and leave as many as you wish. By Allah! Today, whatever you take in the way of Allah, I will not make things difficult for you (that is, I will not stop your hand)."" So the angel said, ""Keep your wealth with you. You three men were only tested. Allah is pleased with you, and displeased with your two companions."""
"2084","Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: By Allah! I am the first person who shot an arrow in the way of Allah, and we used to fight in jihad with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and we had nothing to eat except burnt leaves and acacia (both are wild trees), until one of us would pass stool like a goat does. And now today, the people of Banu Asad (that is, the descendants of Sayyiduna Zubair, may Allah be pleased with him) admonish me for the religion or want to punish me; if this happens, then I am surely at a loss and my efforts have been wasted."
"2085","Sayyiduna Khalid bin Umair Adawi says that (the governor of Basra) Utbah bin Ghazwan (may Allah be pleased with him) delivered a sermon to us. After praising and glorifying Allah, he said: After praise and blessings, know that the world has announced its end? And nothing remains of the world except like the leftover water in a vessel, which its owner drinks. And you are heading towards a home that will never perish, so perform good deeds in your life, because it has been narrated to us that a stone will be thrown from the edge of Hell and it will keep descending in it for seventy years and will not reach its bottom. By Allah! Hell will be filled. Do you find this astonishing? And it has been narrated to us that the distance from one side of the gate of Paradise to the other is a journey of forty years, and a day will come when the gate will be filled with the crowd of people. And I see myself as the seventh among seven people who were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and our food was nothing but the leaves of trees until our mouths became wounded (due to the heat and hardness of the leaves). I found a sheet and tore it into two pieces; I made a lower garment from one piece and Sa’d bin Malik did the same with the other piece. Now, today, there is none among us who is not a governor of a city, and I seek refuge with Allah from considering myself great while being small in the sight of Allah. And indeed, the prophethood of any prophet did not remain forever in the world, rather the effect of prophethood (vanished) after a short time, until its final outcome was that it became kingship. So soon you will see and experience the rulers who will come after us (that the matters of religion, which are the effect of prophethood, will not remain among them and they will become completely worldly)."
"2086","´Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Three things accompany the deceased (to the graveyard). Then two return and one remains. His family, his wealth, and his deeds go with him; so his family and wealth return, and his deeds remain with him. (Therefore, deeds are the true companion; one should strive for them. Children, wealth, and property are only with a person while he is alive; after death, they are of no use, and being attached to them is foolishness.)"
"2087","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Look at the one who is below you (in wealth, beauty, and children), and do not look at the one who is above you (in these things). If you do so, you will not consider the blessings of Allah upon you as insignificant."
"2088","‘Sayyiduna Amir bin Sa’d narrates that Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) was among his camels when his son Umar came (this Umar bin Sa’d is the same one who fought against Sayyiduna Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him) and who ruined his Hereafter for the sake of this world). When Sayyiduna Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) saw him, he said, “I seek refuge with Allah from the evil of this rider.” Then he (Umar) dismounted and said, “You have secluded yourself among your camels and goats and left the people while they are fighting for sovereignty?” (i.e., for caliphate and rule). Sayyiduna Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) struck his chest and said, “Be quiet. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ‘Allah loves the servant who is pious, rich, and (in times of tribulation and discord) hides himself in a corner.’” (And does not ruin his faith. Alas, Umar bin Sa’d forgot his father’s advice.)"
"2089","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty says: I am more free from need of partners than anyone else with regard to shirk (associating partners with Me). Whoever does any deed in which he associates someone else with Me, I abandon him and his act of associating partners. (That is, any worship or deed done for show or fame is not accepted by Allah, it is rejected. Allah only accepts that worship and deed which is done purely for His sake, with no share in it for anyone else.)"
"2090","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever does good deeds to show off to people, Allah Almighty will also make his disgrace known to people on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever acts hypocritically, Allah Almighty will show him (only the reward) but will not give it to him, so that he will have nothing but regret."
"2091","Narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A servant utters a word without realizing its gravity, and because of it he sinks into the Fire as far as the distance between the east and the west (such as complaining about a Muslim or informing against him to the rulers, or slander, or abuse, or a word of disbelief, or mocking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or the Qur'an, or the Shari'ah. Therefore, a person should control his tongue and not speak without necessity)."
"2092","Sayyiduna Suhaib (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The affair of the believer is amazing; there is good for him in every matter, and this is for no one except the believer. If something pleasing happens to him and he is grateful, there is reward in it for him; and if harm befalls him and he is patient, there is reward in that for him as well."
"2093","Narrated from Sayyiduna Suhaib (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Among the people before you, there was a king and he had a magician. When the magician grew old, he said to the king, ""I have grown old, so send me a boy so that I may teach him magic."" The king sent a boy to him, and he used to teach him magic. On the way to the magician, there was a monk (a Christian ascetic, i.e., a priest who had renounced the world). The boy sat with him and listened to his words, and he liked what he heard. Now, when he went to the magician, he would pass by the monk and sit with him, and then when he went to the magician, the magician would beat him (for coming late). Eventually, the boy complained to the monk about the magician's beating, so the monk said, ""When you fear the magician, say that my family kept me back, and when you fear your family, say that the magician kept me back."" The boy continued in this state until one day he came across a large beast that had blocked the people's way. The boy said, ""Today I will find out whether the magician is superior or the monk is superior."" He took a stone and said, ""O Allah, if the way of the monk is more beloved to You than the way of the magician, then kill this animal so that the people may pass."" Then he struck it with the stone, and the animal died, and the people were able to pass. Then the boy came to the monk and told him what had happened. The monk said, ""Son, you have surpassed me. Surely your rank has reached what I see, and you will soon be tested. If you are tested, do not reveal my name."" The boy's condition was such that he would cure the blind and the leper and treat all kinds of illnesses. When the king's companion, who had become blind, heard of this, he brought many gifts to the boy and said, ""All this wealth is yours if you cure me."" The boy said, ""I do not cure anyone; curing is the work of Allah the Exalted. If you believe in Allah, I will pray to Allah, and He will cure you."" The minister believed in Allah, and Allah cured him. He went to the king and sat with him as he used to. The king asked, ""Who restored your sight?"" The minister replied, ""My Lord did."" The king said, ""Who is your Lord besides me?"" The minister said, ""My Lord and your Lord is Allah."" The king seized him and began to torture him until he revealed the boy's name. The boy was summoned. The king said to him, ""O son, have you reached such a level in magic that you cure the blind and the leper and do great things?"" He replied, ""I do not cure anyone; rather, Allah cures."" The king seized him and continued to beat him until he revealed the monk's name. The monk was captured. He was told, ""Renounce your religion."" When he refused, the king sent for a saw, placed it on the middle of his head, and sawed him until he fell in two pieces. Then the minister was summoned and told, ""Renounce your religion."" He also refused, so the saw was placed on the middle of his head and he was sawn until he fell in two pieces. Then the boy was summoned and told, ""Return from your religion."" He also refused. The king handed him over to some of his companions and said, ""Take him to such-and-such a mountain, and when you reach the top, ask him to renounce his religion. If he does, well and good; if not, throw him down."" They took him and climbed the mountain. The boy prayed, ""O Allah, save me from them in whatever way You will."" The mountain shook, and they all fell down, and the boy returned to the king. The king asked, ""Where are your companions?"" He replied, ""Allah saved me from their evil."" Then the king handed him over to some other companions and said, ""Take him in a boat to the middle of the river. If he renounces his religion, well and good; if not, throw him into the river."" They took him. The boy said, ""O Allah, save me from them in whatever way You will."" The boat overturned, and all his companions drowned except the boy, who returned alive to the king. The king asked him, ""Where are your companions?"" He replied, ""Allah the Exalted saved me from their evil."" Then the boy said to the king, ""You will not be able to kill me until you do what I tell you."" The king asked, ""What is that?"" He said, ""Gather all the people in an open field, and crucify me on a trunk. Then take an arrow from my quiver, place it in the bow, and say, 'In the name of Allah, the Lord of this boy,' and shoot the arrow. If you do this, you will kill me."" The king gathered all the people in an open field, crucified the boy on a trunk, took an arrow from his quiver, placed it in the bow, and said, ""In the name of Allah, the Lord of this boy,"" and shot the arrow. The arrow struck the boy in his temple. He placed his hand on the spot and died. When the people saw this, they said, ""We believe in the Lord of this boy, we believe in the Lord of this boy, we believe in the Lord of this boy."" Someone said to the king, ""By Allah, what you feared has happened—the people have believed."" The king ordered trenches to be dug at the crossroads. Trenches were dug, and fires were kindled in them. It was said, ""Whoever does not turn back from this religion (i.e., the boy's religion), throw him into the trenches, or tell him to jump into them."" The people did so, until a woman came with her child. She hesitated to jump into the fire, so the child said, ""O mother, be patient, for you are on the truth (after death there is only peace, so why do you fear the hardship of this world?)."" Imam Nawawi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This hadith proves the miracles of the friends of Allah (awliya), and it also shows that it is permissible to lie in times of necessity, and likewise for the sake of benefit."
